(FIL-02: descriptor is a Number, and for a freshly opened file it is at
 least 3 (fds 0-2 are stdio; a real open never lands below that).
 Also covers: FIL-01 (size is 0 before a write and the byte count after,
 checked BEFORE Close - reading a property after Close reports -1, not
 the true value, which is why every assertion here happens on the open
 handle).
 This is the exact assertion SHAPE the leaf renders: `If <bad> then,
 Print "ASSERT <ID>: ...", Exit 95. Print <subject>` - not just the raw
 value, the failing branch too (proven by the deliberately-broken run
 below).
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-02.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   0
   3
   10
 Then with the first size line changed to `is not 4` (a deliberately
 wrong expectation), to prove a failing assertion is classified
 correctly:
   ASSERT FIL-01: expected 4 got 0
 exit code 95.
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called 'the toolbox' at "vf_scratch/files/fil02.txt".
If 'the toolbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-01: expected 0 got {'the toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the toolbox's size.
If 'the toolbox's descriptor is less than 3 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-02: expected at least 3 got {'the toolbox's descriptor}", Exit 95. Print 'the toolbox's descriptor.
Write "seed bytes" to 'the toolbox'.
If 'the toolbox's size is not 10 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-01: expected 10 got {'the toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the toolbox's size.
Close 'the toolbox'.
